# Korriban, the secret tomb (TSL, 711KOR, to 710KOR), the Exile alone: the
# entrance's scene, the first vision (Malak recruiting the Jedi for the
# Mandalorian Wars: fought at once, Malak's fall fades the others), east
# past the shyrack wyrms, the severed arm's datapad (Jedi Entombed), the
# locked door bashed, the shyrack brood's nest, the dark energy door and the
# second vision (Dxun's minefield: no Dark Path reply, the Exile goes up
# alone and springs the mines, the Mandalorians' charge fought), the Hssiss
# at the junction, the locked door south to the dead Jedi (searched once:
# the quest's end, two Hssiss), north to the third vision (Kreia against
# the companions: protected once for the Light Side, then watched, the
# vision fought out), the last vision ("Revan", the Exile's dark double,
# fought), Kreia's word at Ludo Kressh's sarcophagus, his armband and war
# sword, the crypt rooms' bins, and out the back to the cave, alone.
# Starts at the tomb's door:
#   kjk playthrough tsl @korriban_tomb data/routes/tsl/korriban_secret_tomb.route --god
# Walkthroughs: DSimpson's "Sith Cavern", GameBanshee's "Secret Tomb",
# Kerbow's "Shyrack Cave" 1-5 (context/walkthroughs/tsl/).
# Left: the first vision's two side rooms (north to LowShdLndRubble@3,
# south to TresRakatLock@3, a shyrack wyrm pair each), the minefield's side
# rooms (2nd door north, nothing; south to TresRakatLock@2 and
# LowShdLndRubble@2, a wyrm), the jars and urns: loot for fights.
#
# ASSUMES:
# - The Exile is alone: a_tomb sent every companion to the Ebon Hawk's base
#   (RemoveNPCFromPartyToBase) as 711KOR loaded.
# - Every vision sets the Exile at one hit point at least (SetMinOneHP) and
#   counts a fall a defeat (pc_death: DSP); --god keeps him up.
#   # UNSURE: whether --god keeps the visions' "fell" scripts (pc_death,
#   rev_end start 0) from running at all.
# - The Exile has no Security or Demolitions to speak of (CHOICES.md): the
#   locked doors are bashed, the mines sprung by walking over them.
talk                 # tr_first_enter: the entrance's scene (entrance_cs)
say Enough games, draw your lightsaber and fight! # Malak (malak)
to tr_1st_vision     # the doors shut behind (711_norm_door, 711_1st_door)
talk
fight 30             # Malak; his fall fades the Jedi (k_fab_malak_ud), the doors unlock
to 711_norm_door@1   # east
fight 30             # the shyrack wyrms
use SevrdArm         # the severed arm's datapad (a_jedi_tomb_jrnl: Jedi Entombed)
bash 711_lock_door@1 # "Door{Locked, Bashable}" (DC 28, 120 HP, hardness 5)
# UNSURE: DSimpson only says it is locked and the nest follows; Security at
# DC 28 is out of reach. If the nest's broods break it from inside, `bash`
# is met by the door opened.
fight 30             # the shyrack brood's nest
say This is Dxun... the heart of the Mandalorian crusade. # the Republic Captain (re_flash):
say Only Revan could answer that. # no Dark Path ("The battle is an invaluable
say Not this time, I'll go up there alone. # opportunity", "War calls for blood", "Now charge!")
to tr_kill_shyrak@1  # the dark energy before the door (DarkForce_shyrak)
to wp_2nd_pc         # through 711_2nd_door@1: its OnOpen (tr_pc_god) starts the captain
talk
to G_T_TRAP005@1     # the mines, sprung one by one walking over them: the area's
to G_T_TRAP005@4     # heartbeat (k_hb_check_mines) has the captain charge once no
to G_T_TRAP005@3     # mine is left round check_mines
to G_T_TRAP005@2
to G_T_TRAP005@5     # "{KillsOnEnter}" (a_mine_killnpc: Republic soldiers only)
to G_T_TRAP005@6
# UNSURE: whether the walker steps onto a mine it knows of, and whether a
# trigger's own point is inside its shape; a Demolitions disarm would do the
# same (no goal for it: see korriban.md).
talk                 # "And now we fight!": the Mandalorians rush in (re_flash start 2, a_spawn_mand)
fight 30             # the Mandalorians fade as the vision ends (k_mand_fade_ud)
to 711_2nd_door@3    # east
fight 30             # the Hssiss at the junction
to 711_norm_door@6   # south
fight 30             # the shyrack wyrms
bash 711_lock_door@2 # the dead Jedi's door (Locked, Bashable)
use MidShdLndRubble  # beside it
use jedi_cont        # the Dead Jedi (Dustil Onasi, starved): Jedi Entombed done (a_jedi_jrnl_fin)
fight 20             # the two Hssiss its search calls (searched once only)
say Despite our differences, we need to work together. # Kreia's vision (kreia_vs), first time
say Can I just say something?
say What they are doing is wrong. I will stand with you, Kreia.
say I will protect you, Kreia, so that you may be redeemed later. # (LSP)
to tr_evil_kreia     # north through 711_last_door@2; the way on locked (711_last_door@1)
talk
fight 30             # the companions' visions fall at a blow; Kreia stays
say Despite our differences, we need to work together. # again: the vision watched out
say Can I just say something?
say I think I'll just stand back and watch.
use KreiaEvil
talk
fight 30             # all of them, Kreia too: "Fight with Kreia is done" (711kor_ud case 5) unlocks 711_last_door
# UNSURE: how the vision starts again (DSimpson: "you have to do it again");
# KreiaEvil carries kreia_vs, but her faction after the first fight is not
# known. If she will not talk, drop the first pass and take "I think I'll
# just stand back and watch." the first time (no alignment change).
to tr_last_vision    # through 711_last_door@1: the Exile's dark double (g_darkpc) made
to tr_revan_appears  # "Revan" (revan_fake)
talk                 # (its first reply, no alignment)
fight 30             # the double; 711kor_ud then unlocks the crypt doors and starts rev_end
talk                 # rev_end: "Come back here!", Kreia's warning
say I'm ready to leave. # kreia_tm (not "I am sick of your counsel", -INF)
use sarc_door        # the Ancient Sarcophagus: its OnOpen (tr_kreia_tm) starts Kreia's word
talk
use sith_mummy       # Ludo Kressh's armband and war sword
use TresRakatBin     # the south crypt room (crypt_door@2)
use TresRakatLock@1
use LowShdLndRubble@1 # the north crypt room (crypt_door@1)
exit To_710_2        # through crypt_door@3, back to the cave by the sealed door
module 710kor
party 0,1            # Atton and Bao-Dur back (the party selection, away from the Hawk)
# UNSURE: nothing in 710KOR shows the party screen (k_from_711 only shuts
# SealedDoor): DSimpson's player opens it from the menu. `party` only takes
# the next screen a script shows; the harness needs a way to open it (see
# korriban.md), or the Academy is walked alone.
save korriban_tomb_done
